{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"USN-9155-1","published":"2026-11-18T22:10:58Z","modified":"2026-11-24T14:52:53.445671391Z","related":["UBUNTU-CVE-2026-114938","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-114939","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-114940","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-114942","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-114943","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-114944","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-114945","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-114946"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-114938","CVE-2026-114939","CVE-2026-114940","CVE-2026-114942","CVE-2026-114943","CVE-2026-114944","CVE-2026-114945","CVE-2026-114946","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-114938","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-114939","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-114940","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-114942","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-114943","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-114944","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-114945","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-114946"],"summary":"openjdk-17 vulnerabilities","details":"Albert Yang and Quang Luong discovered that the Compiler component of\nOpenJDK 17 did not correctly handle certain inputs. A remote attacker could\npossibly use this issue to cause a denial of service or execute arbitrary\ncode. (CVE-2026-114938)\n\nIt was discovered that the JGSS component of OpenJDK 17 did not correctly\nauthenticate users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to read\nor modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-114939)\n\nNicholas Carlini discovered that the JSSE component of OpenJDK 17 did not\ncorrectly authorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue\nto read or modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-114940)\n\nIt was discovered that the Libraries component of OpenJDK 17 did not\ncorrectly authorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue\nto cause a denial of service or to read or modify sensitive data.\n(CVE-2026-114942)\n\nIt was discovered that the Hotspot component of OpenJDK 17 did not\ncorrectly authorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue\nto cause a denial of service or to modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-114943)\n\nAlexander Dezhinov, Stanislav Dukhin, Nikita Kozlov, and Binbin Xu\ndiscovered that the Core Java Libraries component of OpenJDK 17 did not\ncorrectly authorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue\nto modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-114944)\n\nIt was discovered that the Libraries component of OpenJDK 17 did not\ncorrectly authorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue\nto modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-114945)\n\nIt was discovered that the Compiler component of OpenJDK 17 did not\ncorrectly authorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue\nto read or modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-114946)\n\nPlease see the following for more information:\nhttps://openjdk.org/groups/vulnerability/advisories/2026-11-17","affected":[{"package":{"name":"openjdk-17","ecosystem":"Ubuntu:Pro:18.04:LTS","purl":"pkg:deb/ubuntu/openjdk-17?arch=source&distro=esm-apps%2Fbionic"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"17.0.21.1+2-1~18.04.1"}]}],"versions":["17+35-1~18.04","17.0.1+12-1~18.04","17.0.2+8-1~18.04","17.0.3+7-0ubuntu0.18.04.1","17.0.4+8-1~18.04","17.0.5+8-2ubuntu1~18.04","17.0.6+10-0ubuntu1~18.04.1","17.0.7+7~us1-0ubuntu1~18.04","17.0.8+7-1~18.04","17.0.8.1+1~us1-0ubuntu1~18.04","17.0.9+9-1~18.04","17.0.10+7-1~18.04.1","17.0.11+9-1~18.04.1","17.0.13+11-2ubuntu1~18.04.2","17.0.14+7-1~18.04","17.0.15+6~us1-0ubuntu1~18.04","17.0.16+8~us1-0ubuntu1~18.04.1","17.0.17+10-1~18.04","17.0.18+8-1~18.04","17.0.19+10-1~18.04.2","17.0.20+8-1~18.04","17.0.20.1+1-1~18.04","17.0.21.0.3+1-1~18.04.1"],"ecosystem_specific":{"availability":"Available with Ubuntu Pro: https://ubuntu.com/pro","binaries":[{"binary_name":"openjdk-17-demo","binary_version":"17.0.21.1+2-1~18.04.1"},{"binary_name":"openjdk-17-jdk","binary_version":"17.0.21.1+2-1~18.04.1"},{"binary_name":"openjdk-17-jdk-headless","binary_version":"17.0.21.1+2-1~18.04.1"},{"binary_name":"openjdk-17-jre","binary_version":"17.0.21.1+2-1~18.04.1"},{"binary_name":"openjdk-17-jre-headless","binary_version":"17.0.21.1+2-1~18.04.1"},{"binary_name":"openjdk-17-jre-zero","binary_version":"17.0.21.1+2-1~18.04.1"},